ah nine times  out of ten nothing happens with the law  it's a lousy law it's a waste of money  and you know be an interesting thing if  we were before we would pass a law if we  privately not publicly privately get  together and pray and ask out what do  you think you know this is the way we're  going Lee we don't know whether it's  right or not we don't ask his opinion  and that's not to say that not this is  not done in Washington's a matter of  fact there's a lot of small groups of  Republicans and Democrats that meet  together my best friend and the Congress  is Congressman Frank will have  conservative Republican we we've been  praying together for 25 years so I find  that you know when you get to know each  other and you build relationships and  you pray together it's pretty hard to go  out right after you pray together and  start yelling and debating and being  partisan and I find that we don't solve  all the problems of the world I mean but  we can't work on problems together and  Frank and I work on problems like human  rights we work on hunger we work on a  lot of things that are that are relevant  to people and we solve some of them now  we don't solve all the problems of  poverty in the world but two things that  come before us the things that we can do  we do  you've said that you think that  humanitarian aid is the best defense or  against terrorism right now can you talk  a little bit about that while you think  that well I think that I I remember  meeting this man in Pakistan who told me  that he sent his son to these schools  these schools that teach hate about us  and about Western nations in and there's  a lot of these schools especially in the  Middle East and in pakistan india etc  and i asked him why do you do this why  would you he said frankly i don't like  what they teach him but I don't have any  money I can't feed him I don't have a  job and they pay for everything and he  gets this free education so this is what  we compete against if we