ergy  costs so to move the food you know many  miles across the ocean is very expensive  the cost of food itself was was terribly  high we had a lot of droughts in various  countries that produce food and then on  top of that we had civil war corruption  all of those things we produce enough  food in the world when I say we the  countries of the world produce enough  food to feed people and so it is a  problem of distribution it's a problem  of not have it's the problem that we  don't have the food the problem is is  why do we have so much food here and not  so much food there and has a lot to do  with the lack of political will has a  lot to do with the lack of spiritual  will you know this issue belongs to  people of faith believers whether  they're Christian or Muslim or Jews I  mean in all of our scriptures there's  nothing talked about more than this and  as I said before it's the second most  talked-about issue it in our Bible so  this issue belongs  yeah among people of faith and we don't  have enough people involved in this the  church needs to be more involved in this  secondly the political will if we could  get the president united states and he's  saying all the right things right now  President Obama he's saying all Hillary  Clinton there they're very matter of  fact I just read a report that they put  out on hunger global global food  security and it's an amazing piece of  work and if they follow through with  this I think it'll really really make a  difference what we've seen in the past  is we go to these conferences and we say  and we've been doing this since the  1970s we say we're going to end hunger  by the year 2015 you know it's always  before it used to be 1995 and then it  was 19 there was two thousand and two  thousand five now it's 2015 now i see  they just upped it to 2025 they said  we're going to cut in half the number of  people that are hungry by the year 2025  you know we go there with all of our top  people our secretaries of state o